{
    "background_story": "Brayan was a thrill-seeking adventurer with a passion for extreme sports. As a professional BASE jumper, he had descended from the world's tallest cliffs and buildings, always pushing the limits of human fearlessness. But his most epic descent was yet to come. Brayan set his sights on the notorious Angel Falls in Venezuela, the highest uninterrupted waterfall in the world. With his custom-made wingsuit, he leaped off the edge of the falls, plummeting 3,212 feet towards the ground at breakneck speeds. The rush was exhilarating, but Brayan's skills and focus allowed him to navigate the treacherous air currents with ease, landing safely at the base of the falls. His record-breaking descent cemented his reputation as one of the world's most daring adventurers.",
